#question(title: [Increasing and one-to-one])[
  #slide-block(title: [Definition])[
    Let $f$ be a function with domain $D$. We
    say that $f$ is #emph[increasing] on $D$
    when

    $
      forall x_1 , x_2 in D, quad x_1 < x_2 ==> f(x_1) < f(x_2) .
    $
  ]

  + Prove that if a function is increasing,
    then it is one-to-one.
  + Use this to show that
    $g(x) = x^5 + 4 x^3 + 2 x + 1$ has an
    inverse.
  + Find $(g^(-1))' (1)$.
]
